title: "What is your approach to automation and testing?"
date: 2019-03-31T15:29:39-04:00
subtitle: "Automated Testing"
draft: false
---

Automated testing, often referred to as "continuous testing" or "continuous integration", refers to the use of software to verify that changes to a codebase have been made safely and properly. It aims to reduce the time and cost of testing so teams can get the work done faster. 

My approach to automation and testing is typically based on the principles of Agile methodology. The key elements in my approach are:

## 1. Continuous Integration (CI):

In Agile software development, the process of merging all developer working copies to a shared mainline several times a day is crucial. This helps teams to share code, learn from each other, and maintain a high-quality master branch. CI tools help reduce errors and waste in the testing process by enabling teams to merge code frequently and to test it immediately after merging.

## 2. Automated Testing:

Almost every software project includes some kind of automated testing. This includes unit tests, integration tests, and end-to-end tests. With automation testing, time-consuming tasks such as setting up the testing environment, executing tests, and analyzing results are typically automated. This allows developers to focus on writing and improving the actual code, rather than manually performing these tasks.

